  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: [DATE]</p>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information <%= storeName %> (the “Platform”) collects, how we use it, and your choices. By using the Platform you agree to this Policy.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information</strong> — your email, display name, and a password (stored only as a secure one-way hash, never in plain text). Sellers may also add a bio and payment handles (Cash App, Venmo, PayPal).</li>
    <li><strong>Listings &amp; content</strong> — titles, descriptions, prices, categories, and any images or files you upload (public preview photos and private delivery files).</li>
    <li><strong>Orders</strong> — the contact info and any note you provide at checkout, the payment method chosen, and the amount.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages</strong> — the content of chats you send to buyers or sellers.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies</strong> — a session cookie (to keep you logged in and remember your age confirmation) and a device identifier cookie (to recognize returning guests so they can continue a conversation). See “Cookies” below.</li>
    <li><strong>Automatic data</strong> — standard server logs such as IP address and browser type, collected by our hosting provider to operate and secure the service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <p>To operate the marketplace: create and manage accounts, publish listings, connect buyers and sellers, show a seller’s payment handle to a buyer at checkout, deliver purchased files after payment is confirmed, enable messaging, and prevent abuse.</p>

  <h2>How your information is shared</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>With other users</strong> — a seller’s payment handle is shown to a buyer at checkout; messages are shared with the other person in that conversation; your display name and listings are public.</li>
    <li><strong>With service providers</strong> — we use third parties to run the Platform: hosting (Render), database (Turso), and image/file hosting (Cloudinary). They process data only to provide their services.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments</strong> — payments happen on third-party apps (Cash App, Venmo, PayPal) directly between users; those apps handle that data under their own privacy policies. We do not receive your full payment details.</li>
    <li>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>We use only the cookies needed to run the site: a login/session cookie and a device-identifier cookie used to keep guest conversations working. We do not use third-party advertising cookies.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We take reasonable measures to protect your information — for example, passwords are stored as salted hashes. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

  <h2>Data retention &amp; your choices</h2>
  <p>We keep your information for as long as your account is active or as needed to operate the Platform. You may request to view, update, or delete your information by contacting us at [CONTACT EMAIL].</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The Platform is for adults (18+) only and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this Policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the “Last updated” date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this Policy or your data? Contact us at [CONTACT EMAIL].</p>

  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:28px;font-size:.85rem;">This document is a general template, not legal advice. Have it reviewed by a qualified attorney before relying on it.</p>
